			"name": "Theology",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A Mars apprenticeship's doctrinal instruction; see Imperium/Skills/Imperial Skills.skl.\n\nDesign: Hard skill; points as above.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus"
			],
			"specialization": "Cult Mechanicus",
			"difficulty": "iq/h",
			"points": 4
		},
		{
			"id": "soIwOjnhGCP0t1JJn",
			"name": "Language",
			"reference": "B23",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The Cult Mechanicus' machine-cant: a clipped, heavily compressed binary/logical language spoken and sub-vocalized between adepts, servitors, and machine spirits alike, ranging from a few ritual phrases a menial picks up to the dense technical liturgy a Magos trades with another Magos.\n\nDesign: Average skill; points as above.",
			"tags": [
				"Mental",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus"
			],
			"specialization": "Binharic",
			"difficulty": "iq/a",
			"points": 4
		},
		{
			"id": "sOTUSF5rcVex679OT",
			"name": "Hidden Lore",
			"local_notes": "Lore: STC and relic recognition from the Mars apprenticeship; see Imperium/Skills/Imperial Skills.skl.\n\nDesign: Average skill; points as above.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus"
			],
			"specialization": "Archeotech",
			"difficulty": "iq/a",
			"points": 4
		},
		{
			"id": "s8h-9-FaU16xbeNwv",
			"name": "Savoir-Faire",
			"reference": "B218",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Court protocol inside the Priesthood: correct forms of address for a Magos or Archmagos, ritual precedence between Forge Worlds and Explorator fleets, and which questions are simply never asked of a superior adept. Not attested under this exact name in the fiction, but the Mechanicus is consistently shown (across Black Library and codex background) to run on a court culture at least as rigid as the Ecclesiarchy's own.\n\nDesign: Easy skill; points as above.",
			"tags": [
				"Mental",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus"
			],
